<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">September 27, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 212</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-09-27T07:00:00Z</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v49.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">&#9878; Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      <span class="cite">F4</span> collapsed from p=0.22 to p=0.03 on Trump's categorical rejection of the Hormuz roadmap on September 26, while <span class="cite">F8</span> opens at p=0.62 on a four-day attack-recurrence window, leaving no active near-term de-escalation pathway on the board.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>&#9888; DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until &ge;20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline &mdash; any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- 2. FORECAST BOARD -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">6 active &middot; last reasoned 2026-09-27 &middot; Sunday cold-start audit</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">NEAR-TERM (&le;72h)</div>
      <div class="forecast-empty-slot">No publishable forecast in this horizon today.</div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7&ndash;30 DAYS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F8</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the IRGC or Iran-affiliated forces conduct a confirmed attack on a commercial vessel or US/allied military asset in the Gulf region before EOD 2026-10-01?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">62%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast &mdash; opened 2026-09-27</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-01</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast opened Sep 27. Priced on September base rate of approximately one named IRGC-attributable incident per seven days (CAPE DAO Sep 23 most recent; EL GAIA preceding). No IRGC restraint signal appeared post-UNGA roadmap rejection on Sep 26. CENTCOM maintains forward posture in Gulf. No tactical pause declared. Four-day horizon makes base-rate calculation relatively mechanical.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if CENTCOM, UKMTO, a named Gulf state defense ministry, or a TIER1 source reports a confirmed IRGC or IRGC-affiliated attack on a commercial vessel or US/allied military asset in the Strait of Hormuz, Persian Gulf, or Gulf of Oman between 2026-09-27 and 2026-10-01 inclusive. Houthi attacks in Hormuz/Gulf of Oman context count; Red Sea-only attacks do NOT.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>CENTCOM or UKMTO advisory, OR two independent TIER1 sources. OSINT-only (AIS anomaly without official confirmation) = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Attacks attributed to unnamed 'unknown actor' without IRGC/proxy attribution confirmed by at least one named authority = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. A mine detonation without confirmed IRGC provenance = AMBIGUOUS. Drone/missile intercept by CENTCOM attributed to IRGC counts as YES regardless of damage.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">UKMTO Gulf advisory issued Sep 28&ndash;Oct 1</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">CENTCOM strike announcement referencing IRGC attack</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran announces tactical pause or restraint signal post-rejection</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F4</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will commercial shipping through the Strait of Hormuz reach &ge;30 vessels/day (7-day rolling average) before EOD 2026-10-03?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">5%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">Δ −17pp from 22% (2026-09-03)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-03</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Three compounding developments: (1) September Hormuz total ~78 commercial transits (~2.6/day average), with Sep 20 recording one transit; CAPE DAO struck by IRGC mine Sep 23 off Musandam &mdash; fourth named commercial vessel event in September. (2) Trump explicitly rejected Iran's seven-day roadmap Sep 26 ("I'm rejecting their deal"), eliminating the only current diplomatic offramp with 6 days remaining. (3) All three indicators CONTRADICTED or NOT_OBSERVED. Mathematical impossibility: reaching 30/day 7-day rolling average from 1&ndash;4/day baseline in 6 days requires approximately 210 transits in an active IRGC mine environment. p_cold=0.02 (Sunday cold-start; 20pp gap confirmed; schema floor applied: p=0.05 per Codex 5-95% rule).</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if any AIS-based ship-tracking source (IMF PortWatch, Straits.live, MarineTraffic, Lloyd's List Intelligence) records &ge;30 commercial transits/day as a 7-day rolling average at any point between 2026-09-03 and 2026-10-03.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>AIS-based tracker + one TIER1 or OSINT confirmation (Bloomberg/Reuters/Lloyd's List).</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If two independent AIS-based trackers diverge by more than 20%, resolution uses the lower reading. Commercial transit = tankers, bulk carriers, container ships; naval/fishing/distress vessels excluded. Single-day spike to &ge;30 without sustained 7-day rolling average &ge;30 = NOT_OBSERVED.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-CONTRADICTED">Sustained 72h halt in Iranian mine/vessel-attack activity</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">P&amp;I war-risk cover reinstated by a named insurer for Hormuz passage</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-CONTRADICTED">CENTCOM or mediator-confirmed Iranian commitment to halt mine deployment</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F9</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will a new confirmed Iran-US indirect negotiating session (mediated, named senior officials) occur before EOD 2026-10-11?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">20%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast &mdash; opened 2026-09-27</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-11</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast opened Sep 27. Trump rejected Iran's UNGA roadmap Sep 26, closing the primary diplomatic track. Residual probability reflects non-zero chance of backchannel resumption through Qatar or Oman; Sep 22 UNGA session established precedent for contact within this conflict period. YES criteria require official US-side confirmation &mdash; not rhetorical &mdash; and named mediator confirmation; opening price capped at 0.20 given Sep 26 rejection.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if two independent TIER1 sources OR one TIER1 plus official mediator readout confirm a face-to-face or proximate shuttle session (not mere written-message relay) between named US senior officials/envoys and named Iranian officials, hosted by a named mediator, between 2026-09-27 and 2026-10-11. An official US-side statement naming the session is required.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two TIER1 (Reuters/AP/AFP/Bloomberg/Al Jazeera) with named principals on both sides, OR one TIER1 plus named mediator government readout (Qatar/Oman/Pakistan/Switzerland MFA).</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Written messages through Qatar without convened session = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Trump public statements about 'semi-negotiating' without Iranian or mediator confirmation of a held session = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Iranian FM statement without named US-side confirmation = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Qatar or Oman MFA announces new mediation session date</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran submits revised Hormuz proposal through mediators</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump publicly confirms another meeting scheduled with named officials</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F5</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Likud win the most Knesset seats (seat plurality) in the October 27, 2026 Israeli election?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">37%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">&Delta; &minus;5pp from 42% (2026-09-03)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-27</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Five late-September surveys: Jerusalem Post aggregation Sep 21&ndash;27 shows Yashar averaging 22.2 seats to Likud's 21.2. Channel 12 records Yashar 23 / Likud 20. Channel 13 shows Likud 18 with Eisenkot bloc at 52&ndash;51 overall. i24NEWS outlier: Likud 27. First-time voters: Yashar 16% vs Likud 14%. p_cold=0.37; gap=5pp, within tolerance (no mandatory flag). Judge retains p=0.37 (2pp above DA's recommended 0.35) for i24NEWS outlier scenario and potential late-campaign Likud consolidation. Sunday cold-start audit.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if official Knesset election results published by the Israeli Central Elections Committee show Likud winning more seats than any other single party in the October 27, 2026 election.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Israeli Central Elections Committee official results, carried by Times of Israel/Haaretz/Reuters/AP.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If Likud and one other party tie on seats: AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO (no plurality). Exit polls alone do not resolve; official preliminary results suffice if published before EOD Oct 27.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-PARTIAL">Polls showing Likud &ge;23 seats, consistently ahead of Yashar in majority of surveys</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Likud bloc forms coalition-eligible alliance pre-election</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Eisenkot/Yashar polling surge &gt;25 seats in majority of polls</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30&ndash;90 DAYS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F10</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will CENTCOM announce a new sustained bombing campaign against targets inside Iran before EOD 2026-11-03 (day before US midterm elections)?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">15%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast &mdash; opened 2026-09-27</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-11-03</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast opened Sep 27. Bloomberg (Sep 26) reported Trump privately told aides he expects to resume large-scale bombing of Iran after the November 4 midterm elections &mdash; placing the most likely US escalation window post-midterms. CENTCOM carrier strike group not yet at surge posture. Iran has not conducted a large IRGC barrage killing US personnel. Diplomatic track formally closed Sep 26 but no US bombing-mandate announcement issued. 37-day window with midterm political constraint produces p=0.15.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if CENTCOM or Pentagon publicly confirms airstrikes against IRGC or Iranian military infrastructure inside Iranian territory on at least 3 consecutive calendar days between 2026-09-27 and 2026-11-03.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>CENTCOM official statement plus two independent TIER1 sources.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Strikes on IRGC-affiliated proxies outside Iran (e.g., Houthi targets in Yemen, militia in Iraq) do not count. A two-day strike sequence pausing and resuming after a 48-hour gap does NOT count as '3 consecutive days.' Israeli unilateral strikes on Iran without US co-announcement do NOT count.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">CENTCOM carrier strike group redeployment to Gulf surge posture</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran conducts large IRGC missile barrage killing US personnel</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump publicly announces formal end to diplomatic track with Iran</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran accepts modified US counter-proposal (diplomacy active)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F11</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the United States and Iran publicly announce a formal ceasefire agreement or new Memorandum of Understanding before EOD 2026-12-31?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">22%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast &mdash; opened 2026-09-27</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-12-31</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast opened Sep 27. Priced on 95-day window, post-midterm US policy review potential (Bloomberg Sep 26 implies Trump reassessment window after Nov 4), and non-trivial probability of a materially revised Iranian proposal under sustained economic compression. Trump's Sep 26 rejection closes the near-term track but not the 95-day horizon. Opening price capped at 0.22 given Trump's documented rejection posture, active IRGC mine campaign, and requirement for named-official confirmation on both sides.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if a joint or parallel public announcement by named senior US officials (Secretary of Defense, National Security Advisor, or President) AND named Iranian officials (President, FM Araghchi, or SNSC) of a formal ceasefire, armistice, or new Memorandum of Understanding for cessation of hostilities is published before EOD December 31, 2026. Carried by two independent TIER1 sources.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Reuters or AP lead story plus one additional TIER1 confirming named officials on both sides. A unilateral US announcement without Iranian confirmation = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Tactical pause lasting fewer than 7 days without named-official framing as 'ceasefire' or 'MOU' = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Ceasefire applying only to Hormuz without broader hostilities halt = AMBIGUOUS &mdash; resolve as YES only if both sides use ceasefire/MOU language in official statements. Iranian FM statement without named US-side confirmation = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Post-midterm US policy review produces new diplomatic mandate</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran submits materially revised Hormuz proposal accepted by US in writing</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump announces end of diplomatic track; renewed bombing campaign begins</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Named mediator announces formal ceasefire framework with both sides present</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">6&ndash;12 MONTHS</div>
