  <!-- 3. DELTA -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive &middot; banned-verb lint enforced &middot; each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>On September 26, President Trump stated publicly "I'm rejecting their deal" regarding Iran's seven-point Hormuz reopening roadmap, transmitted through Qatari intermediaries during the September 22 UNGA session in New York. The roadmap had proposed a seven-day mutual de-escalation window as a precondition for resumed talks; the rejection eliminates the primary diplomatic offramp with six days remaining before the October 3 resolution window. September Hormuz commercial transits totaled approximately 78 vessels through September 26, a seven-day rolling average of approximately 2.6 per day against a pre-war baseline of 85 per day and against the &ge;30/day YES threshold. CAPE DAO, a Marshall Islands-flagged tanker, was struck by what UKMTO assessed as an IRGC mine on September 23 off Musandam &mdash; the fourth named commercial vessel event in September. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span></p>

      <p>The September 22 New York meeting between Iranian Foreign Minister Araghchi and US envoys Witkoff and Kushner, mediated by Qatari representatives, was described by multiple TIER1 sources including Ariana News, Stars and Stripes, Bloomberg, and Axios as the "first talks since June" &mdash; the first convened session since the original MOU framework collapsed in July. No second session has been scheduled or announced by any party or mediator through September 27. CENTCOM maintained a continuous forward naval posture in the Gulf throughout September, with no carrier group withdrawal or formal stand-down in air patrol activity announced. → supports <span class="cite">F8</span> without move</p>

      <p>Five independent Israeli polling surveys conducted September 21&ndash;27 show Yashar (Benny Eisenkot's bloc) holding a lead over Likud across four of the five outlets sampled. Jerusalem Post aggregate polling September 21&ndash;27 recorded Yashar at 22.2 seats and Likud at 21.2. Channel 12 recorded Yashar 23 to Likud 20. Channel 13 recorded an Eisenkot-led bloc at 52&ndash;51 overall with Likud at 18 seats. i24NEWS presented an outlier recording Likud at 27 seats. First-time voter preference data from Channel 12 placed Yashar at 16% against Likud's 14%. The Knesset election is scheduled for October 27, thirty days from the date of this report. → moved <span class="cite">F5</span></p>

      <p>Bloomberg reported September 26 that President Trump privately told advisors he expects to resume large-scale bombing of Iran after the November 4 midterm elections, characterizing the pre-midterm period as one of tactical constraint. No second Iran-US negotiating session has been scheduled or announced following the September 22 UNGA contact; Qatar and Oman MFA offices issued no new readouts on resumed talks through September 27. Iran's rejected roadmap had included a seven-day mutual halt as a precondition for renewed talks, a structure Trump characterized as inadequate. → supports <span class="cite">F9</span> without move, supports <span class="cite">F11</span> without move</p>

      <p>The United Nations General Assembly session saw multiple non-P5 member states &mdash; Turkey, Indonesia, South Africa, and Brazil &mdash; jointly circulate a draft ceasefire resolution on September 25, characterized by Western diplomats as non-binding but intended to maintain multilateral pressure. The resolution had not been put to a formal vote by close of business September 27. No Security Council session on the Iran-US conflict was convened this week; a P5 veto dynamic remains structurally unresolved for any binding UNSC action. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 4. SCENARIO MAP -->
  <div class="section" id="scenario-map">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Scenario Map
