      </div>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (20%):</strong> A new confirmed IRGC attack in the four-day F8 window combined with a US military response before November 4 would activate the 15% pre-midterm bombing probability (F10) and close the 22% ceasefire pathway (F11) before year-end.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (58%):</strong> No new diplomatic session (F9 at 20%) and continued Hormuz closure (F4 at 3%) sustain the current attritional posture through the midterm election date, with neither side accepting the other's preconditions through November 4.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (22%):</strong> Post-midterm US policy review (Bloomberg-reported Trump reassessment) or a materially revised Iranian Hormuz proposal produces the convened session tracked by F9 and advances F11's ceasefire pathway before December 31.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 5. INSIDE IRAN -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode &middot; ~200 words &middot; verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>IRNA and Tasnim News Agency carried extensive coverage of the September 22 New York meeting through the week of September 22&ndash;27, framing Iran's presence as evidence of "readiness for fair negotiations" while simultaneously attributing the failure to reach agreement to US "maximalist demands." Kayhan editorial commentary on September 25 characterized Trump's roadmap rejection as pre-confirmed by what it described as "structural US bad faith" &mdash; a formulation consistent with post-hoc state-media framing. Press TV English broadcast on September 27 led with CAPE DAO wreckage footage alongside commentary on "piracy of the Persian Gulf," attributing the vessel's situation to "US naval aggression forcing civilian ships into dangerous waters." → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>IRGC-affiliated Telegram channels and Fars News Agency both carried statements from IRGC Navy Commander Tangsiri on September 24, describing Hormuz mine operations as "defensive in nature" and pledging "full readiness to defend Persian Gulf territorial sovereignty." Tasnim ran secondary commentary noting that CENTCOM's September 1 strikes on IRGC facilities had not been acknowledged as a deterrent by Iran's leadership; state-media framing consistently avoided any language attributing Iranian operational activity to US military pressure. The Tangsiri statements are the most recent official IRGC-level characterization of ongoing naval posture available before the F8 resolution window opens. → supports <span class="cite">F8</span> without move</p>

      <p>Supreme Leader Khamenei's September 27 address to Revolutionary Guard commanders, carried by IRNA, deployed the standardized "resistance economy" template &mdash; messaging used during sustained sanctions and military pressure periods since 2019. The address made no reference to the September 22 New York meeting or to Trump's roadmap rejection on September 26, consistent with the leadership's documented pattern of not acknowledging backchannel contacts in official public statements. IRNA carried no coverage of the Bloomberg report on Trump's alleged post-midterm bombing plan. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

